# Twin City Small Engine - Global Project Rules

## 1. Design System & Grid Alignment
- **The "Invisible Line" Rule**: All page sections (Headers, Heros, Content) MUST use the exact same max-width container and padding to ensure perfect left-and-right visual alignment.
- **Master Container**: Use `max-w-6xl mx-auto w-full px-4 md:px-8` (or the exact equivalent currently locked into the Hero section) for ALL section wrappers. Never let elements float outside this constraint on desktop.

## 2. Typography & Rhythm
- **H1 (Hero)**: High contrast, heavily weighted, scaling appropriately from mobile to desktop.
- **H2 (Section Headers)**: Must maintain breathing room. Standardize spacing using `mb-4 md:mb-12` to ensure desktop layouts are not cramped.
- **Mobile-First**: Always use base Tailwind classes for mobile, and `md:` or `lg:` prefixes for desktop. Do not use hardcoded pixel values.

## 3. Booking Routing (Strict)
- Do NOT build local lead forms.
- ALL "Schedule" or "Book" CTA buttons must link to the external booking app: `[https://shop-command-phi.vercel.app/book](https://shop-command-phi.vercel.app/book)`
- Must append the correct URL parameter: `?job=Pickup` for shop repairs, and `?job=Tune-up` for at-home services.

## 4. Trust & Brand Elements
- Always maintain high-visibility for the 4 brand logos (Toro, Ariens, Craftsman, Troy-Bilt). Scale them appropriately on desktop.
- Always include the local physical address (702 Southview Blvd, South St Paul, MN 55075) in footers to build local SEO and trust.
